{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And I will bring you, etc. and I will blot them out.</b> It intends that through the agency of Israel's entry those nations would be blotted out. And see what I explained in the verse (Numbers 14:9) ״סָר צִלָּם וְגוֹ׳ וַה׳ אִתָּנוּ״ etc., for the holiness draws out the life-giving portion and leaves behind a lifeless corpse, and this is the sod of what our Sages of blessed memory said (Shabbat 34a): he would cast his eye upon it and it became a heap of bones — for He clarifies and draws out the life-giving portion from its place of embodiment."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "In the Talmudic citation, the Aramaic phrase יָהִיב עֵינֵיהּ בֵּיהּ refers to Rav Yosef; the Or HaChaim appears to connect it to the divine blotting-out of the nations, reading it in the mystical register of extraction of vital force. The final word תַּחֲנוֹתוֹ is rendered hyper-literally as 'its place of embodiment/encampment'; the reading is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:33:01.890115712Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}